    "created_at": "2016-06-07T15:44:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-07T15:44:30Z",
    "body": "In practice CSS only applies to HTML and SVG, both of which have single-target semantics. There's just nothing preventing multiple targets, and such a thing would make reasonable sense.  (For example, HTML could add a dedicated fragment syntax that takes a selector, and let all the targets of the selector match :target.)\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
